From 9efe5da44e7f617f3535169460688df00091c1b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 19:29:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/30] Extend reload-agents to invalidate Skill and Command
 state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0004 added `POST /global/reload-agents` to invalidate the
per-instance Agent registry without disposing InstanceState. That
fixed agents/*.md hot-reload but left the parallel filesystem
catalogs untouched: Skill state (skills/**/SKILL.md) and Command
state (commands/*.md) both also live in InstanceState and stay
cached for the life of the engine.

Adding a SKILL.md to ~/.config/opencode/skills/ and running
`hivemind redeploy` therefore had no visible effect — the skill
wouldn't appear until the engine restarted. Same for new commands.

Extends the existing endpoint to invalidate all three registries:

  - `Skill.reload()` / `Skill.reloadAll()` mirror the Agent pattern.
  - `Command.reload()` / `Command.reloadAll()` mirror the Agent
    pattern. Order matters in the route handler: reload Skill BEFORE
    Command, because Command's init reads `skill.all()` to auto-
    promote skills to slash commands.
  - The `/reload-agents` route handler now calls all three
    reloadAlls. Endpoint name kept (renaming would break the caller
    in `src/hivemind/opencode.py:notify_instance_reload`); the
    summary/description/event schema are extended so the OpenAPI
    doc is honest about the wider scope.

`AgentsReloadedEvent` schema now carries `{instances, agents,
skills, commands}` instead of `{instances, agents}`.
